1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,400
How do you write 56,920 in scientific notation?

2
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:11,200
Move the point left until one digit is in front:

3
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:12,833
4 places.

4
00:00:12,833 --> 00:00:19,167
So 56,920 = 5.692 × 10⁴.

5
00:00:19,167 --> 00:00:22,967
For a small number, move the point right…

6
00:00:22,967 --> 00:00:28,867
…5 places: 9.3 × 10⁻⁵.

7
00:00:28,867 --> 00:00:31,467
Going back? Same move, in reverse.

8
00:00:31,467 --> 00:00:35,967
10⁹: nine places right.

9
00:00:35,967 --> 00:00:41,100
10⁻⁶: six places left.

10
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:43,700
Calculators show this with an E…

11
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:48,433
…E12 means times 10¹².

12
00:00:48,433 --> 00:00:53,1000
The exponent just counts the hops.
